// Package pairing is the device-pairing minting service (device-pairing
// design.md D1/D4-D7): plain domain logic over the store — minting short
// single-use pairing codes, the 5-minute TTL with lazy expiry, the one-shot
// device-token handout, the in-memory per-IP rate limiter, and the SHA-256
// device-token lookup the auth middleware resolves RoleClient with. No HTTP
// lives here; handlers translate its errors (404/409/429) and shapes.
//
// # Public API (6 counted symbols — grouped errors are excluded by the
// counter, the stream grouped-consts precedent)
//
//   - Service: the mechanism, one injectable value. Methods: CreateRequest
//     (rate-limited mint: 128-bit pairing_id + 8-char code, 5-min TTL),
//     Wait (lazy-expiry status poll; hands the device token out exactly
//     once, then consumes), ListPending (the admin review surface),
//     Approve (mints a 32-byte base64url device token, persists ONLY its
//     SHA-256 hash), Deny, Devices, Revoke (DELETE = revoke), LookupToken
//     (hash + indexed store lookup — the middleware branch).
//   - NewService: constructor; the now func is the test clock (nil = time.Now).
//   - Pairing: one pairing request as the admin/API sees it.
//   - Device: one paired device (ID, approval code for recognition, stamp).
//   - WaitOutcome: the poll answer — Status always, Token non-empty ONLY for
//     the approved-and-unconsumed read (single use).
//   - ErrUnknownPairing: unknown pairing OR device id — the handler's 404.
//   - (grouped) ErrRateLimited: per-IP burst exceeded — the handler's 429.
//     (grouped) ErrConflict: approve/deny on a dead request — the handler's
//     409 (expired/consumed/denied).
//
// # Interfaces
//
//   - store (D6): the ONLY storage this package touches — two control tables
//     (pairing_requests, device_tokens) through the store's pairing methods.
//     Clock policy lives HERE (injected now func); the store stays
//     value-agnostic and never sweeps.
//   - api (D1/D3): wired as Deps.Pairing; LookupToken backs the
//     authMiddleware device branch (hash of the presented bearer →
//     RoleClient); handlers map ErrUnknownPairing → 404, ErrConflict → 409,
//     ErrRateLimited → 429.
//
// # Invariants
//
//   - INV1 (capability, not the code): the 8-char code authenticates nothing
//     — it exists for the admin's visual comparison; the unguessable 128-bit
//     pairing_id IS the capability (D4). Knowing the code grants nothing.
//   - INV2 (single use): the device token is handed to the device exactly
//     once — the pickup read flips the request to consumed and the token can
//     never be re-fetched (spec: "Token is handed out exactly once").
//   - INV3 (hash at rest): only the SHA-256 of a token persists; the raw
//     value lives in process memory between Approve and pickup and is never
//     logged, never on the wire to admins (spec: hash-only persistence).
//   - INV4 (lazy expiry): expiry is decided on read against the injected
//     clock — expired overrides pending — never a sweeper goroutine (D6).
//   - INV5 (in-memory limits, D7): the per-IP fixed-window rate limiter and
//     the approve→pickup raw-token handoff reset on restart; accepted for a
//     single-process personal server. A restart cannot resurrect consumed
